-- Named reducer form: fold(threat) and its short spelling threat/ — two spellings of one meaning, forced to agree in public (ex15). Twin of 15-named-reducer.bqn; s64-reducer-spellings adds the scan.
-- threat is a dyadic max, folded pairwise over the scope:
--   Damage @ Enemies   carried
--        12              12
--         7              12    threat(12, 7)
--        30              30    threat(12, 30)
--         9              30    threat(30, 9) — the fold's answer is the final carry
-- threat registers as the dyadic dfn {𝕨⌈𝕩} (the .bqn's ThreatReduce, spelled ⌈ there), folded pairwise as Threat´ by the emitter.
-- Omitted, left to the .bqn twin: fold-direction equivariance, the ¯∞ BQN-identity divergence note, and the no-identity empty-scope row failure — a failed row has no --! spelling.
--! registry ../registries/15-named-reducer.reg

--! out 30
fold(threat) Damage @ Enemies

--! out 30
threat/ Damage @ Enemies
